      'Campaign: the ways between zones follow Diablo II’s. Act I: the Stony Field leads to the Dark Wood through the Underground Passage (no longer directly); the Burial Grounds are walked into from the south of the Cold Plains. Act II: the Valley of Snakes is a dead end; with the Summoner dead, his red portal opens in the Arcane Sanctuary and leads to the Canyon of the Magi. Act III: the Arachnid Lair and the Spider Cavern are two entrances of the Spider Forest, the Swampy Pit is in the Flayer Jungle.',
      'Campaign, Act V: the way to the summit goes through the ice caves, as in Diablo II: Arreat Plateau → Crystalline Passage → Glacial Trail → Frozen Tundra → Ancients’ Way → Arreat Summit; the Frozen River, the Drifter Cavern and the Icy Cellar are dead ends below. Nihlathak’s Temple is no longer an exit of the Frigid Highlands: with Anya freed, her red portal opens beside her in Harrogath, and the temple has its portal back.',
      'Campaign: Act IV is walked on foot, without a loading screen: from the Fortress’s gate to the Outer Steppes, the Plains of Despair and the City of the Damned; the City’s stairs go down to the River of Flame, whose bridge leads into the Chaos Sanctuary. In Kurast, you walk from the Bazaar to Upper Kurast and the Causeway through their gates. When you arrive in a zone by stairs or a cave mouth, you stand at the way back to where you came from.',
      'Campaign: an act opens by difficulty, as in Diablo II: an act walked in Normal is no longer listed at Nightmare’s waypoint until its previous boss dies there.',
