      'Behind the scenes: the base game’s monster levels in waypoint runs and boss farming zones (Tristram, Tal Rasha’s Tombs, Countess, Andariel, Plains of Despair, Pandemonium…) are now those of Levels.txt (Diablo II LoD 1.13c), regenerated from the game files, and Project Diablo 2 levels form a patch in the PD2 mod. Nothing changes in game.',
      'Behind the scenes: the base game’s monster fidelity (resistances and immunities, regeneration, boss life and damage) is now that of Diablo II LoD 1.13c (MonStats, SuperUniques), regenerated from the game files, and Project Diablo 2 values (key holders, Andariel, ubers and Diablo Clone: resistances, life, life leech) form a patch in the PD2 mod. Nothing changes in game.',
      'Behind the scenes: the base game’s treasure classes (monster and boss loot) are now those of Diablo II LoD 1.13c (TreasureClassEx), regenerated from the game files, and loot specific to Project Diablo 2 (boss, Ancients and uber tables, Worldstone shards, puzzle pieces, Pandemonium items, player count of the “no drop” formula) is part of the PD2 mod. Nothing changes in game: same rolls, same items.',
      'Behind the scenes: the base game’s monster levels per zone are now those of Diablo II LoD 1.13c (Levels.txt), regenerated from the game files, and Project Diablo 2 levels (33 zones, many of them level 85 in Hell) form a patch in the PD2 mod. Nothing changes in game: same zone levels, same recommended levels.',
      'Behind the scenes: the base game’s unique items and sets are now those of Diablo II LoD 1.13c, regenerated from the game files, and Project Diablo 2 values (properties of 354 uniques, set bonuses, Bul-Kathos’ Death Band) form a patch in the PD2 mod. Nothing changes in game: same uniques, same sets, same bonuses.',
      'Behind the scenes: the base game’s item bases, runes and gems are now those of Diablo II LoD 1.13c, regenerated from the game files, and Project Diablo 2 values (damage, defense, sockets, rune effects) form a patch in the PD2 mod. Nothing changes in game: same items, same values, same sockets.',
      'Behind the scenes: Project Diablo 2 endgame maps (37 map zones and 46 map affixes, map generation, events, loot, Cube map recipes, map menu and merging, map bosses) are now part of the PD2 mod instead of the base game. Nothing changes in game: same maps, same affixes, same bosses, same loot.',
      'Behind the scenes: Project Diablo 2 skill numbers (damage, durations, synergies and per-hard-point tables of all 219 skills) are now part of the PD2 mod instead of being merged into the base game. Nothing changes in game: same values at every level, same tooltips.',
      'Behind the scenes: content specific to Project Diablo 2 (Worldstone and corruption, Larzuk’s puzzle, uber access items, map items and orbs, quivers, sunder charms, 47 PD2 uniques and their Cube recipes) is now loaded as a separate mod, active for every existing character. Nothing changes in game: same items, same recipes, same order in the recipe book.',
      'A save holding an item unknown to this version (item from a missing mod, damaged save) no longer crashes when loading. The item is set aside, untouched, inside the save (a message says so when the game starts) instead of blocking the game; normal saves are unchanged.',
      'Saves now use format 7: each character records its ruleset (“PD2” for every existing character, nothing else changes), in preparation for mods. A save written by this version no longer opens in an older version of the app: update all your synced devices (a device still on the old version shows “reload the app” instead of opening the character).',
      'A new character now starts in the Rogue Encampment (Act I), and after reconnecting you reappear in the last town you visited (Encampment, Lut Gholein, Kurast Docks, Fortress or Harrogath) instead of always returning to Harrogath. Older saves stay in Harrogath until you next visit another town.',
      'Diablo II import: the “Checking files…” step now shows a progress bar (file name and MB read), or an animated bar while it prepares.',
      'Updates: “Install now” now shows a window with a progress bar and the current step (saving, installing, restarting) instead of a screen that looks frozen.',
      'Importing a save: the file is now checked (size, structure, known items) and rejected with a clear message if it is damaged or tampered with; valid saves import as before.',
      'Guild vault: a received item that looks invalid (unknown item, absurd values) is now refused instead of corrupting your save.',
      'Accessibility: icon buttons now have a name for screen readers, and the system “reduce motion” option is respected by the interface.',
      'Credits: the screen now states where the game data comes from (tables re-created from Diablo II data and community wikis, with attribution; unaffiliated fan project).',
      'English: about a hundred texts that were still in French are now translated (save import, Diablo II import, sign-in, stash and Cube messages), and singular plurals (“1 item”, “1 result”) are now translated too.',
