    en: [
      'Diablo II archives are checked at import: a truncated or zero-preallocated archive (interrupted download, same size as the original) is detected before anything is built, with the empty area (in MB), the number of files affected and a few names. Required archive: building waits, with a “Choose the file again” button; optional archive: ignored with a warning. Each archive’s MD5 is computed during the copy and compared with the reference distribution (“different version” is never an error: other editions exist). Settings › Diablo II files: “Check” column, MD5 and “Full verification”; the copyable diagnostic has a “check:” line per archive.',
      'Corrupted maps: the line changed by corruption is marked with a red asterisk (*) in the tooltip.',
      'Maps: the action column’s “Corrupt” button stayed greyed out (“See Upgrade”) even when the Upgrade menu offered it. It now uses the same check (map not corrupted, World-stone shard, in town) and opens the same confirmation; when greyed out it says why.',
      'Action-menu confirmations (Corrupt, Reroll / Remove affixes, Dungeon, Socket, Sockets…): they now open as a small centred window over a dimmed background, always visible without scrolling the list, with big Confirm / Cancel buttons (48 px). Esc or a tap on the background closes the confirmation.',
      'Next-zone preparation fixed: a zone was only apparently “prepared” (its campaign map was never built). It now counts only when ALL its assets at the current quality are ready; its map data is built and loaded first, a failing zone is retried then reported with the reason, and the menu refreshes live (MB generated, zones prepared, pause reason). Every sentence of the menu is now translated.',
      'Missing archives: the summary lists, per category, the required archives (measured: d2data, d2exp, d2char) and optional ones (sounds, Patch_D2) with their status; a missing archive is named (“Required: d2xxx.mpq”) with an “Add d2xxx.mpq” button in Settings, on the wait screen and on the error screen. Each archive can be added alone, at any time.',
      'Public version: no pre-made character any more (the level-99 test Sorceress no longer exists in the public version). The alternative character appearance (skin) was removed; a character that had it goes back to its normal look.',
      'Diablo II graphics now default to high resolution on every device (phones included): “Auto” = High, except on a device with 2 GB of memory or less, or almost full storage (under 700 MB free) where it stays economy, with a message. An explicit choice (Economy or High) is kept; what was already generated in economy stays in use and is replaced by high resolution as you play, without blocking. The display texture budget still lowers, sheet by sheet, what would not fit in memory.',
      'The next zones are now prepared in advance in the background, in progression order (Tristram first, then Acts I to V: maps, floors and decor, monsters, effects). Low priority, paused when the game slows down, when a loading screen or menu is open, when the page is hidden, or when data saver or a low battery require it; resumes after a reload; can be turned off in Settings › Advanced.',
      'Settings › Advanced › “Diablo II graphics & files”: a summary by category (interface, icons, characters by class, monsters, decor and maps by act, effects, sounds) with MB used, progress, estimated time left, “Generate now” and “Clear” per category, “Generate everything”; list of MPQ archives (required and optional) with what each one brings and “Add this file” without selecting everything again (verified copy into OPFS).',
      'Damaged Diablo II files on the device: a badly decoded MPQ sector no longer leaves silent zeros (the cause of “DC6 version 0”), it becomes an explicit error; the incomplete-interface diagnostic names each unreadable D2 file with its position, compression, sectors and the first bytes read.',
      'Interface wait screen: when the interface is incomplete (e.g. 48 images out of 82), it lists the missing required images and the expected count; a partial interface is never marked ready any more (the failure names the missing or unreadable Diablo II files) and the copyable diagnostic includes these details.',
      'Screen “Preparing the Diablo II interface…” stuck after the import (“Retry” doing nothing): cause found, the interface was marked ready while its images were missing from the cache, and “Retry” requested nothing. The screen now repairs itself (re-read, then rebuild), shows live status (phase, files, queue, workers, last error), “Retry” answers at once (“Retrying…”) and really restarts (failures forgotten, workers replaced, service reopened); a crashed or never-opened worker now leaves a readable error. With no progress for 20 s: a clear message, “Copy error details” and “Verify / repair files”; “Choose my Diablo II files…” really re-runs the preparation.',
      'Diablo II file copy is now verified: every written chunk is read back and compared with the original (partial writes are looped, a bad chunk is rewritten, otherwise a clear “file is damaged” error) with a “Verifying files…” bar and stored fingerprints. Settings › Diablo II graphics: “Verify copied files”. On a data error (“DCC: invalid signature”…), the error screen offers “Verify / repair files”: an intact copy means the problem is elsewhere; otherwise it is removed and copied again with verification.',
      'Character select screen (local graphics): always the Diablo II screen, never the original one (it waits for the interface with “Retry” if missing); in portrait the scene stays whole and the buttons move to a bottom bar, big enough for a finger.',
      'Pre-game menus (file import, character select) now work in portrait: the “rotate your device” prompt only appears once in game.',
      'Loading: a preparation failure no longer blocks the start. The screen shows the real error (file and technical message) with “Retry” (only what failed), “Continue anyway” (the game starts, what is missing keeps its fallback and is generated in the background) and “Copy error details” (diagnostic to send me). One automatic retry happens before the error is shown; the “Continue” button works again (the original wait screen was covering it).',
      'Interface generation uses less memory (images encoded one at a time); files picked one by one: a file that became unreadable is reported immediately.',
      'Install: “Install the app” button (pre-game screens and Settings; “Share → Add to Home Screen” hint on iOS); the service worker is registered at launch, so the app is installable even when loading is stuck.',
      'Diablo II file import: you can now pick the files one at a time; the ones already chosen are remembered, just add the missing ones.',
      'Local Diablo II graphics, no fallback: once you import your files, the game no longer shows any original sprite or floor. A loading screen waits until everything is ready, in the order it is needed (interface, icons, map, floors and walls, character and equipment, monsters, objects, effects, sounds) with the current step and the estimated time left; it is short on PC and longer the first time on a phone, then everything stays on the device.',
      'A run waits for the Diablo II maps to be ready (“Preparing the Diablo II maps…” at the waypoint). If the files are gone or storage is full, a clear message says what to do (guided re-selection). The import screen is now in English and reminds you that you must own Diablo II: Lord of Destruction.',
    ],
