    en: [
      'Public version: no guild stash and no save synchronization; your characters stay on this device (export them from Settings to move them).',
      'Diablo II graphics generated on your device (Settings › Advanced › “Diablo II graphics on this device”, experimental): you provide your own d2data.mpq, d2char.mpq and d2exp.mpq files and the game builds the graphics in the background, on demand, without sending anything anywhere. The game starts right away with its original sprites, then swaps them in as they become ready (“Preparing graphics…”).',
      'The files are copied to the device (≈ 770 MB, resumable after an interruption) so you never have to select them again; if storage is full or an archive is missing or unreadable, a clear message tells you what to do. The economy tier is picked automatically on phones; “Generate everything now” and “Clear the generated graphics” are available in Settings.',
      'Diablo II maps generated on your device: zones (floors, walls, collision) are built from your files, the town right away, the others in the background, the images of each zone on your first visit; campaigns are prepared from the waypoint (“Prepare the maps”). Placed decor (torches, standards) is not available; Settings › Advanced › “Diablo II maps” turns them off.',
      'Diablo II graphics start screen: on the first launch of a public version, a large card explains what to do — “I have Diablo II: import my files” (which files to choose, where to find them, nothing is uploaded, space and duration). Pick several files or a whole folder, copy progress, clear errors, automatic resume if the files are already on the device; a discreet link lets you play with the replacement graphics.',
      'Diablo II sounds and music generated on your device (optional, experimental): besides the three graphics files you can provide d2sfx.mpq (sound effects), d2speech.mpq (character voices), d2xtalk.mpq (expansion voices) and d2music.mpq (zone music). Nothing is prepared in advance: each effect, voice and music track is decoded the first time it is heard, then kept on the device (the first effect waits about ten milliseconds, a music track one to a few seconds). Sounds already used stay available even without the files. Without these archives the game keeps its replacement sounds. Copying the sound archives (≈ 1 GB) is a separate choice; add and clear them in Settings › Advanced.',
    ],
