      'Inventory adapted to square and unfolded foldable screens (Galaxy Z Fold): the panel, tooltip and menu fit entirely; the gold field is no longer covered by the Cube button.',
      'Loot announcements are queued: no more overlapping messages after a boss (3 at most, rarest first, duplicates grouped "×N").',
      'Consistent ground-item rarity: one rule for display and announcements. High runes (Vex and above) get a giant orange-red beam, sparks, a pulsing "★ Rune ★" label and a dedicated sound; exceptional items (elite uniques and sets, unique charms and jewels, Worldstone shards, essences, unique maps) get a tall beam and a golden label.',
      'Diablo II-style movement: your character, mercenary, minions and monsters now slide and sidestep around corners, pillars and tile edges instead of snagging. Your mercenary paths around walls to follow you and snaps back next to you if stuck. Click-to-move routes keep a wider berth around corners.',
      "Monsters: every monster's attack speed now matches Diablo II (original animation lengths). Venom Lords, skeletons, goatmen, succubi, Nihlathak, Mephisto and most melee monsters struck too fast; their hits (and therefore Mana Burn drain) are now slower.",
      'Monster groups now appear off-screen even on large screens (unfolded Galaxy Z Fold): no more monsters popping in right in front of you.',
      'Interface: the Stash, Merchant, Skills, Character and Mercenary panels now fit both the width and the height of the screen (unfolded foldables, square screens): no more cut-off columns, truncated tabs or menu overlapping the content.',
      'Monsters by zone: the Durance of Hate is populated with vampires (Ghoul Lords) around Mephisto again instead of Act 5 Death Lords. Super uniques now appear once and only in their own zone (Rakanishu, Beetleburst, Snapchip Shatter); no more doubled tomb guardians; small Nightmare and Hell zones keep regular monsters; Frigid Highlands, Halls of Vaught and Throne of Destruction monsters now match Diablo II; Normal levels of the Act 5 runs aligned with PD2.',
      'Lightning and Chain Lightning: new, clearly visible forked lightning animation; Chain Lightning now arcs from target to target with a Diablo II lightning strike on each monster hit.',
      'Grand Charms with +1 to a skill tree (for example +1 Sorceress Fire skills): treated as exceptional items on the ground (tall beam, golden label, announcement).',
      'New “Corrupt” button on items (bag, stash, equipped, bag maps) in town: same cost and odds as the Cube recipe (1 Worldstone Shard), with a confirmation showing the outcome odds and brick risk. Setting “Confirm before corrupting an item” to corrupt in one tap.',
      'Vex rune icon fixed: it reused the Um rune image (a flaw in the base Diablo II files, fixed by the official patch).',
      "Endgame maps: no more squares! Every map now has its own larger shape, generated each time it is opened: jungle clearings, islands in lava, a village with its graveyard, a ruined city, a marketplace, a canyon, a lava-lined switchback road, a river with fords, craters, an abyss crossed by bridges, a hedge maze, a cross-shaped tomb, symmetrical temple and cathedral, the Throne's spiral, canal sewers, catacombs, the Bastion's walls… The boss waits at the far end, events hide in side pockets, and the minimap reveals itself as you explore.",
      'Separate respec: one button for stats only (Character sheet) and one for skills only (skill tree), besides the full reset. Free as before if the setting is on; otherwise each one uses a respec.',
      'One shared stash for all your characters: items from your old personal pages are moved there automatically (a backup copy is kept). Runes, gems, materials and maps stay per character for now.',
      'Loot filter: new Highlight tab — pick items from the whole database, they show on the ground in the color you choose, and can stay visible despite the filter; "Highlight this item" from the tooltip.',
      'Shared stash: 12 pages instead of 6 (expandable up to 40 instead of 20 when migrating old personal stashes).',
      'Lighter sync: saves are now uploaded after 3 minutes of inactivity (at most every 10 minutes of continuous play), when closing or switching away, and only if the content changed. If the service is unavailable, the game retries at growing intervals and never touches your local saves.',
      'Loot filter: scrolling now works (highlight list, preview, plus a fix for every scrollable panel on touch screens). The Highlight tab now lists the whole item database (~1,300 entries) by category — weapons, armors, helms, shields, gloves, boots, belts, jewelry, uniques, sets, runewords, runes, gems, charms, misc — with search, checkboxes, Select all / Deselect all, a color applied to the selection, and 80-row pages. The highlight list grows from 60 to 300 items.',
      'Stash: pages are shown in windows of 5 with "‹" and "›" (the 12 pages overflowed under the menu on square screens).',
      'Filter highlight: search also matches English names (for example "frostwind" finds "Vent de givre") when the game is in English.',
      'Corrupted items: a small red dot "●" now appears before every line added or changed by corruption (added properties and sockets), with a legend on the "Corrupted" line.',
      'Maps: new Upgrade button on every map (bag, stash, map stash). Orbs, fortification, catalyst, heroic standard, scarab and corruption in one click, with cost and stock shown, without using the Cube (in town). Setting to confirm irreversible operations.',
      'Sockets from the item menu: Pierce (Larzuk) in one click (once per difficulty, with the expected result and a confirmation) and every Cube recipe that adds sockets (Ral + Amn + Amethyst, Puzzle Box and Piece...), straight from the bag, stash or worn item, without opening the Cube. Item actions are now grouped under two menus next to the main action: Crafting (sockets, socket, corrupt, upgrade a map) and Manage (Cube, mercenary, drop, highlight). Only one menu is open at a time; click elsewhere or press Escape to close it.',
      'Sockets: a "Craft a Puzzle Box (10 pieces)" line in the item\'s Crafting menu, with the piece count; the box (not loose pieces) is needed to pierce a unique or set item.',
      'New “Character appearance” setting: an alternative skin (removed since) replaces the character. Mercenary and summons are unchanged.',
      "Stash: new layout. The tabs move to the top; Character, Stash and item details are always side by side, even on a landscape phone, with a fixed, compact action column on the right (Equip/Put in stash/Take, Cube, Corrupt, Crafting, Mercenary, Highlight, Drop). Unavailable actions stay in place, greyed out, with the reason in a tooltip. Double-tap or right-click: quick action. Stash maps are now a selectable list. The merchant's Buy back tab is reachable again.",
      "Maps: new Merge block in the stash's Maps tab. Merge all your normal T1 or T2 maps in one click (3 → 1 of the next tier with the Cartographer's Orb) or compress them for free (3 → 1 of the same tier) to free up space; bag maps can be stored in the map stash in one go.",
      "Maps: monsters are now only immune to the elements announced on the map. Hell's natural immunities and the species' immune variants are brought down to 75% resistance, and monster resistance affixes no longer create immunity: only the map's \"Immunities\" line (30% of the zone's monsters) and immunity affixes grant it.",
