      'Map bosses are real bosses now: much more life, a large health bar at the top of the screen, 3 to 5 special skills per map (projectile rings, sweeps, meteor or lightning rain, walls, charges, auras, poison pools, teleport strikes, stacking venom, a shield you break by killing its guardians), all marked on the ground before they hit. Phases at 75, 50 and 25%, and an enrage if the fight drags on. They drop real boss loot: several items including a rare, often a unique or set item, a rune and a gem. The Baal and Duriel reflections in dungeons no longer come five at a time.',
      'Ground items: the socket count now also shows for superior, damaged and magic items (for example "Superior Flail [2]"), and the "Eth." prefix comes before the name of ethereal items. The English "Pick up" button no longer scrambles quality and text.',
      'Maps: the portal back into the map no longer disappears when you return to town after killing the boss (loot and monsters kept, no new boss or second reward); it goes away when you start another run.',
